Why not?  That's a cursed portable hole, and it should be "in your
backpack".  It makes things randomly fall out onto the floor.  The
portable holes should be cartoon-style, not AD&D-style.  They're not
dimensional portals like bags of holding are - they're temporary dig
effects.  You can also throw one on the ground to go down a level (if
there is a room below you) and the size of the portable hold determines
how many levels you can go through before there has to be a room.  I
remember one cartoon where a portable hole led all the way to Hell.

An uncursed portable hole will, of course, allow you to throw it on the
wall and walk throug it, then remove it from the other side.  It can also
be used to get off a cursed object (as in "Who Framed Roger Rabbit", where
Eddie uses one to get a magnet out from around him, stuck to a metal
object) but the object becomes "A cursed holey blindfold" or such. 
Naturally, the hole disappears, becoming an integral part of the object. 

A blessed portable hole, of course, is a little more versatile.  It can be
taken off an object (like a cursed suit of armor) and also does not make
the characteristic "SMACK!" or "SNAP!" noise of a portable hole being
used.

A suggestion:  a chain should be able to be used with a gem to make an
unspelled amulet.  Wield it and enchant weapon.  Then it asks what spell
to store in it.  You can put any spell or intrinsic you have - to make an
amulet of that.  Amulets of life saving are made with blessed dilithium
crystal, blessed rustproof chain, and an intrinsic of regeneration AND a
spell of extra healing.  You lose the intrinsic, of course, and it is
considerable physical exertion to force a magic that is in your body to be
stored in an object.

